{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790173482,"nonce":"g8vKC/jr8+0Y0EdtcnMsU6v4vv8=","title":"Derive plugin enums and native event mappings from Rust declarations","message":"Ordinary Rust enums should generate Caribou metadata and direct shared-heap conversions without requiring Serde or duplicate plugin enum declarations. Winit events also need declarative projections rather than handwritten nested conversion matches.\n\nImplemented locally: caribou_abi::PluginEnum derive, enum TypeName registration in plugin!, unit/tuple/named-field variants, nested ordinary Rust enums, owned strings, source From mappings with explicit patterns/projections/fallbacks, and input/payload GC rooting. The window plugin now queues ordinary Rust enums and encodes them only during poll; existing mouse and cursor behavior is preserved and Other mouse buttons are supported.\n\nValidation: ABI and derive tests, a headless winit mapping test, and all four plugin integration tests pass. Integration tests also pass under ASH_GC_STRESS=1 WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1, including nested Haxe/Wren round trips and shared buffers. Haxe data, plugin, and window fixtures rebuilt. GUI execution was not tested.\n\nNo new runtime layout or ABI version is required. The existing Zyntax shared-heap transfer gap remains tracked in c5751252b0e8b1e9a019fb93e9db98caf8bc2a9dc5bee7b2f890bfac10344c23.","files":null}]}